  "notes": "### Added\n\n- In Reviews, close a pull or merge request without merging it, or reopen a closed one, from the button beside Comment at the end of its Overview.\n- In Reviews, a conflicting request offers *Rebase onto* on its banner. If the forge cannot replay it, the banner says to rebase locally; any other refusal, such as no push access, shows the forge's message.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- On Linux, Nori starts again on Debian 13, Ubuntu 25.10, Fedora 43, Arch and other distributions with a recent libcurl, instead of crashing at launch.\n- In Reviews, a GitLab merge request that is behind or conflicts with its target shows its banner when it opens, not up to 4 seconds later.\n- In Reviews, a GitLab rebase that succeeds after a failed one is no longer reported as refused.",
